To achieve a blurred card with a non-blurred locker icon, you'll need to structure the HTML so that the icon is positioned outside the blurred card element. Here's how to implement it:

### Step 1: Update the HTML Structure
Wrap the card in a container and add the locker icon as a sibling element:

```html
<div class="card-container">
  <div class="info-card locked-card" id="card7">
    <div class="title">Locked</div>
    <div class="value">99</div>
  </div>
  <span class="lock-icon">🔒</span>
</div>
```

### Step 2: Add CSS Styling
```css
/* Container to hold the card and icon */
.card-container {
  position: relative; /* Creates a positioning context for absolute children */
  display: inline-block; /* Adjust as needed */
  /* Add any other container styles */
}

/* The blurred card */
.locked-card {
  background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  filter: blur(6px);
  position: relative;
  /* Keep other styles like padding, margin, etc. */
}

/* The locker icon */
.lock-icon {
  position: absolute;
  top: 5px; /* Adjust based on desired position */
  right: 5px;
  font-size: 24px; /* Adjust size */
  color: #000; /* Adjust color */
  z-index: 1; /* Ensure it's above the card */
}
```

### Explanation:
1. **HTML Structure**:
   - The `.card-container` wraps both the blurred card and the locker icon.
   - The `lock-icon` is a sibling of the card, not a child, so it isn't affected by the blur.

2. **CSS**:
   - The `.card-container` uses `position: relative` to allow absolute positioning of the icon.
   - The `.locked-card` retains its blur and background styles.
   - The `.lock-icon` is positioned absolutely within the container, placed on top of the card using `z-index`.

### Result:
- The card and its content (title and value) are blurred.
- The locker icon remains sharp and unblurred, positioned over the card.

### Demo:
```html
<style>
.card-container {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-block;
  padding: 10px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
}

.locked-card {
  background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  filter: blur(6px);
  padding: 20px;
}

.lock-icon {
  position: absolute;
  top: 10px;
  right: 10px;
  font-size: 24px;
  color: red;
  z-index: 1;
}
</style>

<div class="card-container">
  <div class="info-card locked-card" id="card7">
    <div class="title">Locked</div>
    <div class="value">99</div>
  </div>
  <span class="lock-icon">🔒</span>
</div>
```

This approach ensures the icon remains sharp while the rest of the card is blurred. Adjust `top`/`right` values in `.lock-icon` to position the icon as desired.

