---

### Option 1: Using Flexbox (Recommended)
Add these styles to the **parent `div`**:
```css
.parent {
  /* Make the parent a flex container */
  display: flex;

  /* Center horizontally */
  justify-content: center;

  /* Center vertically */
  align-items: center;
}
```

This will center all child elements (including the `img`) perfectly in the middle of the parent.

---

### Option 2: Using Grid Layout (Simpler Shorthand)
Add these styles to the **parent `div`**:
```css
.parent {
  /* Make the parent a grid container */
  display: grid;

  /* Center both vertically and horizontally */
  place-items: center;
}
```

The `place-items: center;` property is a shorthand for `align-items: center` and `justify-items: center`.

---

