1. We initialize left, right, and ans. The variable ans keeps track of the best index found so far (starting with –1 indicating no valid index has been found).

2. We perform a binary search. If arr[mid] is strictly less than the target, we update ans to mid and search in the right half (to see if there’s a later element that still satisfies the condition).

3. If arr[mid] is greater than or equal to target, we search the left half.

4. Finally, if an element was found, its index is returned; otherwise, we return –1.

This solution runs in O(log n) time, which is efficient for large sorted arrays.

