            yield Label(self.filename, classes="filename")
            yield Button("Delete", id=f"delete_{self.filename}")

    def on_button_pressed(self, event: Button.Pressed) -> None:
        if event.button.id.startswith("delete_"):
            self.remove()

class FileListApp(App):
    CSS = """
    FileEntry {
        height: 2;
        background: $surface;
        border: round $primary;
        padding: 0 1;
        margin: 1;
    }

    .filename {
        width: 100%;
        text-align: left;
    }
    """

    def compose(self) -> ComposeResult:
        with Static(id="file-list"):
            for filename in ["document.txt", "image.jpg", "notes.md"]:
                yield FileEntry(filename)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    app = FileListApp()
    app.run()
```

This code does the following:

1. Creates a `FileEntry` class that represents each file entry:
   - Uses a Horizontal container to place the filename label and delete button side by side
   - The delete button has an ID that includes the filename for identification
   - Handles button presses to remove the entire file entry when the delete button is clicked

2. The main `FileListApp` class:
   - Contains a CSS style block to make entries look like buttons with borders
   - Uses a Static container to hold all file entries
   - Provides an initial list of sample files

Key features:
- Each file entry looks like a button with a delete button on the right
- Clicking the delete button removes the corresponding file entry
- Automatically styles the entries to look like interactive elements
- The layout adapts to terminal size changes

To use this code:
1. Make sure you have Textual installed (`pip install textual`)
2. Run the script and you'll see a list of files with delete buttons
3. Click the delete buttons to remove entries

The "button within button" effect is achieved by:
- Wrapping the filename and button in a container styled like a button (`FileEntry`)
- Placing the actual delete button inside this container
- Using CSS to style the container to look like a button element

You can customize the initial filenames by modifying the list in the compose method of `FileListApp`.

